  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pod100-500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Pod 502.06 Controlled Drug Prescription Health and Safety Program",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pod 502.06 Controlled Drug Prescription Health and Safety Program.\n\n(a) Prescribers required to register with the program under RSA 126-A:91, or their delegate, shall query the program to obtain a history of schedule II-IV controlled substances dispensed to a patient, prior to prescribing an initial schedule II, III, and IV opioids for the management or treatment of this patient’s pain and then periodically and at least twice per year, except when:\n\n(1) Controlled medications are to be administered to patients in a health care setting;\n\n(2) The program is inaccessible or not functioning properly, due to an internal or external electronic issue; or\n\n(3) An emergency department is experiencing a higher than normal patient volume such that querying the program database would materially delay care.\n\n(b) A licensee shall document the exceptions described in (a)(2) and (3) above in the patient’s medical record.\n\nSource. #12149, eff 3-25-17; ss by #14616, eff 7-1-26, EXPIRES: 7-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pod100-500.html"
}
